{
  "$comment": [
    "Authored block uniform contract shared by the TypeScript WebGPU renderer and the",
    "Emscripten C++ renderer. scripts/generate-cpp-uniforms.mjs turns this into both",
    "cpp/src/generated/authored_block_uniforms.h (C++ struct + static_asserts) and the",
    "WGSL struct the C++ block shader declares, so an offset can only drift in one place.",
    "Field order is the WGSL/std140 order; offsets are explicit and validated by",
    "tests/cpp-block-parity.test.ts against WGSL uniform-address-space packing rules.",
    "",
    "Names that also exist in the TS FragmentUniforms (src/webgpu/shaders/block/uniforms.ts)",
    "carry `tsField`, and the test asserts the semantics line up. The C++ block is a strict",
    "subset: it omits TS-only state (dissolve field, column heights, audio levels) that the",
    "C++ path has no producer for yet.",
    "",
    "goldTint/goldShade/mapParams mirror the TS AuthoredMaterialParams block (@binding(14)). TS keeps them in a separate uniform buffer because its fragment uniforms are already at their binding-size limit; the C++ path folds every uniform into binding 0, so they live here. Values are generated from public/block-material.json into authored_block_material.h, which is where both renderers get them from."
  ],
